#### Connection

This step sets up the analytics environment in R to query Google BigQuery data. It loads the required packages, authenticates access to Google BigQuery using an approved Google account, and then creates a live database connection to the dataset in BigQuery. The connection is configured to bill query costs to our Google Cloud project, enabling us to run scalable queries on the raw GA4 event data directly from R.

```{r}
library(bigrquery)
library(DBI)
library(dbplyr)
library(tidyverse)
library(glue)


#| eval: false
#| echo: true
# Method 2: Authenticate with specific email
bq_auth(email = "cerenunal18@gmail.com")
# Verify authentication worked
bq_user()
# Should show your Google account email

#| eval: true
#| echo: true
# Set up your project ID
# This is your Google Cloud project ID
# Find it at: console.cloud.google.com
